{'symbol': 'REGN', 'date': '2022-11-30 08:05:00', 'title': 'EVKEEZA® (EVINACUMAB-DGNB) SBLA FOR CHILDREN WITH ULTRA-RARE INHERITED FORM OF HIGH CHOLESTEROL ACCEPTED FOR FDA PRIORITY REVIEW', 'text': 'IF APPROVED, EVKEEZA WOULD BE THE FIRST AND ONLY TREATMENT OF ITS KIND TO HELP CHILDREN AS YOUNG AS 5 YEARS OLD CONTROL DANGEROUSLY HIGH LEVELS OF LDL CHOLESTEROL CAUSED BY HOMOZYGOUS FAMILIAL HYPERCHOLESTEROLEMIA TARRYTOWN, N.Y. , NOV. 30, 2022 /PRNEWSWIRE/ --\xa0REGENERON\xa0PHARMACEUTICALS, INC.\xa0(NASDAQ: REGN) TODAY ANNOUNCED THE U.S. FOOD AND DRUG ADMINISTRATION (FDA) HAS ACCEPTED FOR PRIORITY REVIEW THE SUPPLEMENTAL BIOLOGICS LICENSE APPLICATION (SBLA) FOR EVKEEZA® (EVINACUMAB-DGNB) AS AN ADJUNCT TO OTHER LIPID-LOWERING THERAPIES TO TREAT\xa0CHILDREN AGED 5 TO 11 YEARS WITH HOMOZYGOUS FAMILIAL HYPERCHOLESTEROLEMIA (HOFH).'}